senses.gloss:
जनित्र, अम्, n., Ved. a birthplace, place of ori-
gin, home; origin, generative or procreative matter;
N. of a Sāman; (आणि), n. pl. parents, relatives.

जनुस्, उस्, n. (Ved. Nom. m. जनूस्, Acc. जनु-
षम्, Inst. जनुषा), birth, production, descent;
nativity; birthplace; a creature, being; creation;
genus, class, kind; जनुषा, ind., Ved. by birth,
from birth (e. g. जनुषान्ध, blind from birth),
by nature, naturally, originally, essentially, necessa-
rily, &c.

जन्तुक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. his
descendants; (आ), f. lac, gum; a kind of Asa Fœtida;
[cf. जतुका.]
